#
# cppcheck suppressions for scripts/run_static_analysis.sh: one check id per
# line, each with its reason. A finding in our own code is fixed, or
# suppressed inline at its line with the reason beside it (--inline-suppr);
# only what cannot be fixed in this tree is listed here. Every entry, and
# every inline suppression, has its row in docs/misra.md's "Tool
# suppressions" (tests/firmware/test_misra_register.py). An unreferenced
# function is not cppcheck's to find: scripts/ast_census.py reads the image's
# translation units together (unusedFunction, suppressed here until FW-20,
# read one file at a time and could not follow member-function pointers).

# The standard and ESP-IDF headers are not given to cppcheck (it reads the
# fake ESP-IDF of the host harness for the project's own includes only).
missingIncludeSystem
# An inline suppression that a later fix made unnecessary is not an error.
unmatchedSuppression
# A raw loop over a fixed table is kept where the algorithm would hide a
# bound or an early exit the code relies on (MISRA C++:2023 favors the
# explicit loop over a callable here; docs/misra.md).
useStlAlgorithm
# A parameter named after the accessor of the value it carries (setProfile(
# Profile profile) beside profile()) is deliberate. It hides no variable:
# -Wshadow, which the compiler gates, and MISRA C++:2023's hiding rule are
# about variables, and a member function is not one.
shadowFunction
